00:08:16.957 --> 00:08:20.792
(dark music)

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:24.720
The cat disappears for a little while Coraline&nbsp;
is speaking to The Other Mother. It’s pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:28.320
clear that this is because the two are&nbsp;
enemies. He avoids her for most of the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:32.160
but he’s also quite familiar with her, enough&nbsp;
to suggest that she is probably trying to lure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:37.280
Coraline in because she wants something to love or&nbsp;
possibly something to eat. He also knows that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:41.360
can’t resist a good game and suggests Coraline&nbsp;
challenge her to one to win back her parents.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:45.040
This is another reason I think he must have&nbsp;
had his own encounter with her in the past.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:48.320
He also recommends that Coraline get some&nbsp;
sleep ahead of the long day tomorrow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:52.400
and that’s exactly what she does. Before she gets&nbsp;
up the next morning the Other Mother goes out to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:56.800
try to fix up the secret passageways that the cat&nbsp;
uses to enter and exit her world. This tells me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:01.280
that The Beldam and the cat’s fear of each other&nbsp;
may be mutual. Afterall, The Beldam’s true form&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:05.360
is a spider-like creature, and cats are known&nbsp;
to eat spiders. There are multiple occasions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:08.880
where she refers to the cat as “vermin”. It’s&nbsp;
also possible that she’s just trying to seal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:12.960
up the entryways because her minions are rats,&nbsp;
another species that cats are known to devour.

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:17.440
When Coraline goes outside that morning, she runs&nbsp;
into her furry friend. “Its fur stood straight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:21.280
out from its body and its eyes were wide, while&nbsp;
its tail was down and between its legs. It did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:26.000
not look a happy cat.” It sounds to me like he’s&nbsp;
very much on edge when he’s in The Other World.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:29.680
As Coraline explores, the cat explains&nbsp;
there’s nothing to find outside of the house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:33.920
because The Beldam hasn’t bothered to create it.&nbsp;
This line is obviously book-only, as the garden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:38.880
is a more important location in the movie. And the&nbsp;
2009 game! Together, they loop all the way around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:43.280
the small world, back to the house, which the&nbsp;
cat describes using an analogy to a spider web.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:48.000
“Spiders’ webs only have to be big enough to&nbsp;
catch flies.” Again, this demonstrates familiarity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:52.320
with the ancient antagonist. She hasn’t yet&nbsp;
revealed her spidery true form to Coraline.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:56.720
The cat is unimpressed with The Beldam’s attempts&nbsp;
to keep it out. He also claims there are ways in and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.720 --> 00:10:01.200
out that she does not know about. He also catches&nbsp;
a rat and explains that they are spies for her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:05.200
He tortures the rat before eating it, adding&nbsp;
that some people see the tendency of a cat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:08.960
to play with its prey as a merciful one&nbsp;
because sometimes the prey will get away.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:12.720
This analogy is no mistake, he’s suggesting&nbsp;
that Coraline’s game of hide and seek with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:16.960
The Beldam could result in her getting away,&nbsp;
if she plays her cards right. The cat then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:21.520
disappears behind a tree to presumably eat the&nbsp;
rat, or deposit it somewhere in the real world.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:25.200
At this point, the cat kind of disappears for&nbsp;
most of the rest of Coraline’s game against her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:29.360
Other Mother. We don’t know if he’s hiding away&nbsp;
from his evil adversary, or just keeping an eye&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:33.360
on Coraline’s progress from a distance. Her goal&nbsp;
is to find the souls of the three ghost children&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:37.360
and her parents, and she’s managed to recover two&nbsp;
of the three souls, but the leader of the rats,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:40.720
who I’ll just call, The Big Rat, is in the&nbsp;
process of getting away with the third.

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:45.280
What the cat does is the perfect example of why&nbsp;
Coraline is definitely part of the horror genre.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:50.720
He catches the rat in his sharp teeth, decapitates it, and stops&nbsp;
the soul marble with one paw. This one is toned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.720 --> 00:10:54.480
down a little bit in the movie, but the film has&nbsp;
no shortage of horrifying moments of its own.

00:10:54.480 --> 00:11:00.800
– [cat] I don't like rats at the best of times,&nbsp;
but this one was sounding an alarm.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:04.320
The cat is unsurprised to learn that&nbsp;
The Beldam doesn’t plan to let them go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:07.520
even if Coraline finds her parents to&nbsp;
win the game. He’s also the first to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:11.680
notice that the house is losing its 3D form&nbsp;
and flattening out into a crude drawing.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:15.440
Coraline thanks him for his help, and says he&nbsp;
can leave, and she’ll see him back at home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:18.080
but he tells her that the ways in&nbsp;
and out of this world are gone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:21.280
which seems to be very unsettling&nbsp;
for him. Coraline tries to pet him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:25.360
and realizes he’s trembling and his heart&nbsp;
is beating hard. So she promises to bring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:28.880
him home with her and carries him into the&nbsp;
house, where the Other Mother is waiting.

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:33.440
The cat stiffens upon seeing her. Coraline tricks&nbsp;
the Other Mother into opening the passageway&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:37.440
between the two worlds, the Link Between Worlds,&nbsp;
if you will, in order to prove that her parents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:42.080
aren’t there. Coraline has a plan, but the cat clearly isn't in on it. She does her best Alinity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:46.080
and throws the cat at The Other Mother; it lands&nbsp;
on her head and flails at her with claws and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:50.640
teeth. As Coraline grabs the snowglobe containing&nbsp;
her real parents, the cat bites The Beldam’s cheek&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:55.280
and draws the black tarry blood that flows within&nbsp;
her. After throwing a claw to her face, he joins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:59.120
Coraline in a sprint to the corridor that bridges&nbsp;
the two worlds, and after slamming the door on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:03.680
their enemy, urges Coraline to run with him --&nbsp;
the last words he would ever say to her outloud.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:07.520
They get back to the Jones family’s drawing&nbsp;
room, where Coraline apologizes for throwing him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:12.080
and he seems to accept this apology by purring,&nbsp;
licking her finger and falling asleep in her lap.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:16.000
He wakes up before Coraline and waits by the&nbsp;
door when Coraline’s parents come inside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:20.400
in order to quickly run away before they can do or&nbsp;
say anything. I’m guessing he didn’t want to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:24.880
any chances with how they’d react to an unfamiliar&nbsp;
animal in their house, or he just didn’t trust any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:28.400
creature vaguely resembling Coraline’s mother&nbsp;
at this point. Can you really blame him?

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:32.400
Again, the cat disappears for a week, the time&nbsp;
that Coraline spends defeating the Beldam’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:36.320
dismembered hand that had scuttled its way into&nbsp;
the real world. When they saw each other again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:40.560
The cat winked at her and rolled onto his back,&nbsp;
allowing Coraline to scratch the fur on his belly.

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:44.640
Through their journey together, the two had&nbsp;
become friends. The witch had found her cat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:49.120
and more importantly, Coraline kind of has someone&nbsp;
suitable to spend time with now. Wybie is not in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:52.800
the book at all, so she has no one to play&nbsp;
with or talk to, and the other adults in her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:56.400
world don’t really listen to her. I think&nbsp;
that’s part of what made The Other World,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:59.600
where the cat could talk, so appealing&nbsp;
for Coraline at the beginning of the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:03.200
but as she learned, she doesn’t need verbal&nbsp;
cues to communicate with this animal.

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:07.040
And that’s the end of the cat’s story in the&nbsp;
book. In the movie, things are a bit different,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:10.560
because the cat seems to be attached to Wybie&nbsp;
in the beginning, because he feeds it, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:13.280
the final shot shows him disappearing&nbsp;
through one of the hidden portals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:17.680
presumably back into The Other World, which may&nbsp;
have been reopened after The Beldam’s defeat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:22.160
I talk about Wybie, the Beldam, Coraline, and&nbsp;
others in their own Horror History episodes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:25.920
For all my Coraline character breakdowns,&nbsp;
hit that playlist on the left. But first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:29.920
make sure you subscribe to CZsWorld for new&nbsp;
horrors every week, ring the deathbell and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:38.640
select all notifications and I will see you&nbsp;
in the next one. Assuming we both survive.

